        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Saint-Mihiel, World War I\n- People: John J. Pershing\n- Organizations: American Expeditionary Force, United States Army, French troops, German forces\n- Roles: commander of the American Expeditionary Force, senior United States Army officer\n\nFacts:\n- John Joseph \"Black Jack\" Pershing was born on September 13, 1860, and died on July 15, 1948.\n- John J. Pershing was a senior United States Army officer.\n- John J. Pershing served as commander of the American Expeditionary Force on the Western Front during World War I from 1917 to 1918.\n- The Battle of Saint-Mihiel was a major World War I battle fought from September 12 to September 15, 1918.\n- The Battle of Saint-Mihiel involved the American Expeditionary Force and 110,000 French troops under the command of John J. Pershing of the United States against German positions.",
